wasmux demo rootfs
==================

This is the initramfs that arch/wasm unpacks into the rootfs at boot.
It contains no executables: the wasm port cannot fork or execute
userspace, so /init is a documentation-only placeholder.  Instead of
exec'ing it, kernel_init() runs the resident shell
(arch/wasm/kernel/shell.c), which is the interactive interface of the
port.
